   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The inner expression is \\( u = 3 - x^{2} \\), with \\( u' = - 2 x \\), and \\( \\frac{d}{du}\\arctan u = \\frac{1}{1 + u^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "inverse trigonometric derivative with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = - \\frac{2 x^{3}}{\\left(3 - x^{2}\\right)^{2} + 1} + 2 x \\arctan{\\left(3 - x^{2} \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = -2, \\( u = -1 \\) and \\( u' = 4 \\), so \\( h'(-2) = \\pi + 8 \\).",
